{"info":{"author":"AIMarket","author_email":null,"bugtrack_url":null,"classifiers":["Intended Audience :: Developers","License :: OSI Approved :: Apache Software License","Programming Language :: Python :: 3","Topic :: Security :: Cryptography"],"description":"# attested-memory\n\nPython client and CLI for [Attested Memory](https://attestedmemory.net/) — verifiable memory\nfor AI agents. Every call is signed by your own Ed25519 **actor** key; the private key never\nleaves your machine. A memory you read is checked here, on the client, against the\n`content_hash` the hub recorded, so a changed text is refused instead of trusted.\n\n```bash\npip install attested-memory\nattested-memory init                      # your actor key → ~/.config/attested-memory/actor.json (0600)\nattested-memory trial                     # 7-day personal key, bound to that actor\nattested-memory write \"Supplier terms\" \"Net 30, EUR, signed 2026-09-01\" --tag finance --source contract-17\nattested-memory search supplier\nattested-memory read mem_…\n```\n\n```python\nfrom attested_memory import Actor, Client\n\nactor = Actor.generate()              # or Actor.load(\"actor.json\")\nclient = Client(actor)\nclient.start_trial()                  # or Client(actor, api_key=\"ask_…\")\nunit = client.write(\"Supplier terms\", \"Net 30\", tags=[\"finance\"])\nclient.read(unit[\"id\"])               # raises IntegrityError if the text does not match its hash\n```\n\nWhat is checked where:\n\n| | where |\n|---|---|\n| your identity (`did:actor:` + SHA-256 of your public key) and a one-time signed proof per request | client signs, server verifies |\n| the text of a memory matches its `content_hash` | **this client** |\n| `truth` (supported / contested / rejected) and `provenance` (attested receipt) | reported by the hub |\n\nActor proof v2 binds the recipient audience, method, final path, ordered query\npairs and SHA-256 of the exact body bytes. A captured proof cannot authorize a\ndifferent request. Nonces are persisted by the service, including across worker\nrestarts. `Client` handles these targets automatically; direct callers must pass\n`audience`, `method`, `path` and the exact `body` bytes to `Actor.proof_headers`.\nLegacy identity-only proofs are refused. See the\n[wire contract](../../../docs/actor-request-proofs-v2.md).\n\nEnvironment for the CLI: `ATTESTED_MEMORY_HOME`, `ATTESTED_MEMORY_URL`, `ATTESTED_MEMORY_API_KEY`.\n\nApache-2.0. Source: [alexar76/attested-memory](https://github.com/alexar76/attested-memory) (`clients/python`).\n","description_content_type":"text/markdown","docs_url":null,"download_url":null,"downloads":{"last_day":-1,"last_month":-1,"last_week":-1},"dynamic":null,"home_page":null,"keywords":"agent-memory, ai-agents, ed25519, memory-poisoning, provenance, verifiable","license":null,"license_expression":"Apache-2.0","license_files":["LICENSE"],"maintainer":null,"maintainer_email":null,"name":"attested-memory","package_url":"https://pypi.org/project/attested-memory/","platform":null,"project_url":"https://pypi.org/project/attested-memory/","project_urls":{"Homepage":"https://attestedmemory.net/","Source":"https://github.com/alexar76/attested-memory"},"provides_extra":["dev"],"release_url":"https://pypi.org/project/attested-memory/0.2.0/","requires_dist":["cryptography>=41","pytest>=8; extra == \"dev\""],"requires_python":">=3.9","summary":"Client and CLI for Attested Memory: write, search and read verifiable AI-agent memory under a signed Ed25519 actor identity.","version":"0.2.0","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},"last_serial":43157326,"ownership":{"organization":null,"roles":[{"role":"Owner","user":"aleksandr.artamokhov"}]},"releases":{"0.1.0":[{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":{"sha256":"0485e518d0e124fa2846f83ec6f19705b4ab88d60f6b850e9e42271573dcafb5"},"digests":{"blake2b_256":"b316046b3c7d5b903915838ae89f94ce4ab2c79d8b86c574d38d7c1849353cde","md5":"30634e3e71abd69a9a469465debf3fe3","sha256":"7530adc222e21236f25f815ae6ccc36aafb4feb571bda9077787bfd352f04ff2"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"attested_memory-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"30634e3e71abd69a9a469465debf3fe3","packagetype":"bdist_wheel","python_version":"py3","requires_python":">=3.9","size":9391,"upload_time":"2026-10-11T14:03:16","upload_time_iso_8601":"2026-10-11T14:03:16.702920Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/b3/16/046b3c7d5b903915838ae89f94ce4ab2c79d8b86c574d38d7c1849353cde/attested_memory-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null},{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":false,"digests":{"blake2b_256":"70d30f9f3ac831e453a0761c1bea38b4b0324bb40403c0ec49a67fa4b9baad38","md5":"06a839833087c2c57bf3250bc141da8c","sha256":"0f826bfa7a74dcdb2ab8820cdf36ff7d704ba06948dbf68a10321841efa96b65"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"attested_memory-0.1.0.tar.gz","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"06a839833087c2c57bf3250bc141da8c","packagetype":"sdist","python_version":"source","requires_python":">=3.9","size":9099,"upload_time":"2026-10-11T14:03:17","upload_time_iso_8601":"2026-10-11T14:03:17.992997Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/70/d3/0f9f3ac831e453a0761c1bea38b4b0324bb40403c0ec49a67fa4b9baad38/attested_memory-0.1.0.tar.gz","yanked":false,"yanked_reason":null}],"0.2.0":[{"comment_text":null,"core-metadata":{"sha256":"4420241863622e9861a6f0b5019a2dba1f19873014aafcf9a897b16dc50c6f3a"},"digests":{"blake2b_256":"9ee7eb5f91311be1de9eba661c8595afd432570d4e70155ab7e7f3ba6641c4da","md5":"c3ebb72b48193fd2d13310c0d8696ef9","sha256":"08bdf52de756c14c4fbece8836f8122bec38c3bf1ed7bdd477a7ad597c560cfe"},"downloads":-1,"filename":"attested_memory-0.2.0-py3-none-any.whl","has_sig":false,"md5_digest":"c3ebb72b48193fd2d13310c0d8696ef9","packagetype":"bdist_wheel","python_version":"py3","requires_python":">=3.9","size":10397,"upload_time":"2026-11-03T19:46:29","upload_time_iso_8601":"2026-11-03T19:46:29.580232Z","url":"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/9e/e7/eb5f91311be1de9eba661c8595afd432570